From 050f9107e3b448758d3428cb38638057448dae8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maxolgi <maxolgi@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:35:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] avformat: add libquicsrt protocol

QuicSRT is SRT live streaming over HTTP/3 WebTransport. This protocol
exposes it through the libquicsrt client library (--enable-libquicsrt,
pkg-config "quicsrt >= 0.1.0").

URL syntax: quicsrt://host:port?stream=NAME[&cert_hash=HEX][&pki=0|1]
[&latency_ms=N]. Direction decides semantics: an output publishes the
named stream toward the gateway, an input subscribes to it, so the same
URL works verbatim on both sides.

cert_hash pins the gateway certificate by the SHA-256 of its DER form
(64 hex chars), the way browsers pin self-signed WebTransport servers.
pki=1 selects normal PKI validation and is the default when no cert
parameter is given; cert_hash and pki are mutually exclusive. All
parameters are also available as AVOptions, and a parameter given in
the URL query overrides the option value (http.c convention); unknown
query parameters are rejected. String values are percent-decoded.

The payload is MPEG-TS bytes: the library frames them into 188-aligned
SRT live messages of at most 1128 bytes (6 TS packets). Reads deliver
one message at a time through an internal bounce buffer, so any caller
buffer size works; writes loop over the library's partial-accept
contract, resuming from the first unaccepted byte.

Opens are a single attempt and fail fast, bounded by the library's
connect timeout (default 10 s). A stalled peer fails a dataless read
after 15 s and a backpressured write after 30 s (defaults; the generic
rw_timeout option overrides both when set). The AVIO interrupt
callback is honored in the read and write loops and short-circuits
graceful teardown at close.

Signed-off-by: maxolgi <maxolgi@proton.me>
---
